<title>SINGAPORE: IOC sells Bombay low aromatic naphtha to Glencore.</title>
<headline>IOC sells Bombay low aromatic naphtha to Glencore.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) has sold by tender 20,500-tonnes of low aromatics naphtha (LAN) to Swiss trader Glencore at a discount of $25.38 a tonne to spot Japanese quotes, industry sources said on Monday.</p>
<p>The tender was awarded on a free-on-board (fob) Bombay basis for lifting on January 23-25.</p>
<p>In its last LAN tender from Bombay, IOC sold 25,000-tonnes lifting January 6-8 at $22.50 per tonne below Japanese spot quotes, fob.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3093)</p>
